README.md:# Workboard
README.md:Requires Node.js 22.22.1. No dependency installation is needed.
README.md:Run:
README.md:```sh
README.md:PORT=8080 DB_PATH=./data/workboard.sqlite npm start
README.md:```
README.md:Open http://localhost:8080. Defaults are port 8080 and `data/workboard.sqlite`.
README.md:The server binds to `0.0.0.0`; `GET /health` returns `{"status":"ok"}`.
README.md:Projects and their tasks (including completion state) are stored in the configured
README.md:SQLite file, which must be retained across restarts. Open a project to create tasks,
README.md:toggle completion, and filter by All, Open, or Completed. The project list defaults
README.md:to Active; select Archived to open or restore archived projects. Archived project
README.md:pages are read-only, including the rename controls. Active projects can be renamed
README.md:with New project name and Rename project without changing their URL or tasks.
README.md:Each task row has New task title and Rename task controls; renaming preserves
README.md:its order, ownership and completion state. Each task also has a Task priority
README.md:selector (Low, Normal, High), defaulting to Normal. Priorities persist independently
README.md:and survive renaming. Archived task rename and priority controls are disabled.
README.md:Project rows show completed/total task counts. Existing
README.md:SQLite databases are migrated automatically to preserve projects and tasks.
README.md:Verify:
README.md:```sh
README.md:npm test
README.md:```
README.md:Tests use a temporary SQLite database outside the repository and check health,
README.md:validation, ordering, safe rendering, navigation, task ownership, completion,
README.md:filtering, archive/restore, completion summaries, database migration, read-only
README.md:archived pages, project and task rename validation and identity preservation,
README.md:task priority defaults, migration, independence and validation, and persistence
README.md:across restarts.
